    "id": "p41-q54-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "54",
    "prompt": "Show that\n$$\\frac{1\\times3\\times5\\times\\cdots\\times(2n-1)}{2\\times4\\times6\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)}=\\frac1{4^n}\\binom{2n}{n}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac1{4^n}\\binom{2n}{n}$.\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by the even-factor product $2\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)=2^n n!$.",
      "worked": "Write $O=1\\times3\\times\\cdots\\times(2n-1)$ and $E=2\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)$. Then $E=2^n n!$ and $OE=(2n)!$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1\\times3\\times\\cdots\\times(2n-1)}{2\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)}&=\\frac{OE}{E^2}\\\\\\frac{1\\times3\\times\\cdots\\times(2n-1)}{2\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)}&=\\frac{(2n)!}{(2^n n!)^2}\\\\\\frac{1\\times3\\times\\cdots\\times(2n-1)}{2\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)}&=\\frac1{4^n}\\frac{(2n)!}{n!n!}\\\\\\frac{1\\times3\\times\\cdots\\times(2n-1)}{2\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times(2n)}&=\\frac1{4^n}\\binom{2n}{n}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
